      "type": "text",
      "duration": 3.0,
      "content_summary": "Lesson title"
    },
    {
      "id": "CK12-MATH-006-U002",
      "label": "Definition: simplest form (text)",
      "type": "text",
      "duration": 24.0,
      "content_summary": "A fraction is in simplest form when the numerator and denominator share no common factor other than 1. To simplify, divide both by their greatest common factor (GCF)."
    },
    {
      "id": "CK12-MATH-006-U003",
      "label": "GCF method diagram (image)",
      "type": "image",
      "duration": 15.0,
      "content_summary": "Diagram showing 12/18 with factor trees for 12 and 18, highlighting shared factors 2 and 3, GCF=6."
    },
    {
      "id": "CK12-MATH-006-U004",
      "label": "Worked example: 12/18 simplified (text)",
      "type": "text",
      "duration": 30.0,
      "content_summary": "12/18 ÷ 6/6 = 2/3. Full division shown step by step, confirming 2/3 cannot be simplified further."
    },
    {
      "id": "CK12-MATH-006-U005",
      "label": "Practice problems (text)",
      "type": "text",
      "duration": 18.0,
      "content_summary": "Four fractions to simplify: 8/12, 15/20, 9/24, 14/35."
    },
    {
      "id": "CK12-MATH-006-U006",
      "label": "Lesson root: Simplifying Fractions",
      "type": "text",
      "duration": 3.0,
      "content_summary": "Top-level document container."
    }
